[I] A system daemon to allow session software to update firmware

[T] fwupd is a system daemon that aims to make updating firmware on Linux
[T] automatic, safe and reliable. It allows session software and the
[T] fwupdmgr command line tool to update device firmware, e.g. from the
[T] Linux Vendor Firmware Service (LVFS), using a large number of device
[T] plugins.

[U] https://fwupd.org

[A] LVFS by Richard Hughes
[M] René Rebe <rene@exactco.de>

[C] base/tool
[F] CROSS

[E] add jinja2
[E] add flashrom
[E] opt vala
[E] opt gi-docgen graphviz
[E] opt libftdi1
[E] opt openimageio
[E] opt systemd

[L] LGPL
[V] 2.1.10

[D] 50788e851880bf3244ec3ca4ea309809bb37ae54e58b6b970d04b90b fwupd-2.1.10.tar.xz https://github.com/fwupd/fwupd/releases/download/2.1.10/

pkginstalled gobject-introspection || var_append mesonopt ' ' -Dintrospection=disabled
var_append mesonopt ' ' '-Defi_binary=false -Dplugin_uefi_capsule_splash=false'
var_append mesonopt ' ' -Dtests=false
